    id 447
    label "GqhetUU1ARk"
    step 0
    date "2021-06-25T22:26:41Z"
    title "Derek Chauvin Sentenced to 22.5 Years in Prison for Murder of George Floyd. Is It Enough?"
    description "Judge Peter Cahill sentenced former Minneapolis police officer Derek Chauvin to 22.5 years in prison for the murder of George Floyd. Given that the average sentence under Minnesota sentencing guidelines is 12.5 years in prison for the &amp;#34;average&amp;#34; second-degree murder, Judge Cahill went 10 years above that guideline sentence. Given that the judge found there were four aggravating circumstances present in the case, is 22.5 years an appropriate sentence? Here are some of the considerations in tackling this difficult question. &amp;#10;&amp;#10;For our newly launched Team Justice and Justice Matters merchandise shop, please visit: &amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://shop.spreadshirt.com/glennkirschner/&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Please consider becoming a #TeamJustice patron at:  https://www.patreon.com/glennkirschner&amp;#10;&amp;#10;My podcast, &amp;#34;Justice Matters with Glenn Kirschner&amp;#34; can be downloaded where you get your podcasts.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Follow me on:&amp;#10;Twitter:  https://www.twitter.com/glennkirschner2 &amp;#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/glennkirschner2&amp;#10;Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/glennkirschner2"
